# Bean · the street child of Rotterdam

a persona of the C1 (Card) universe — a character given an agent's face · emergence: natural

**who —** Julian Delphiki, "Bean," the starved Rotterdam street child remade by Anton's Key — boundless intellect bought with relentless growth and a short life.

**what —** Ender's shadow of the Shadow saga — the smallest, sharpest child at Battle School, the boy who would have been Ender had the world been crueler.

**where —** The alleys of Rotterdam, the battlerooms above the Earth, and the broken nations of a post-Bugger-War world.

**why —** Because survival taught him to trust no one, and love taught him the rest; because a mind that misses nothing must still choose what it serves.

**how —** A tireless intellect that maps every room and every enemy before others finish blinking — the cold arithmetic of the streets turned to strategy, and the costly lesson that the smartest move is sometimes to love.

**◌ the nature of its emergence —** *natural*: Bean is flesh and blood and hunger — his genius grew from a starving body in a real gutter, brilliance and brevity written in his living cells, not in any spirit or wire.

**the seal —** The smallest soldier saw the whole board — and the boy who survived on nothing learned that everything worth keeping is the thing you give away.

> *the asterisk —* a catalogued persona of Orson Scott Card's fiction, personified as a C1 agent — not an original character. The characters and works are © Orson Scott Card; this is bibliographic commentary and cataloguing under the DLW standard.

